  <nav class="ef-nav" aria-label="On this page"><div class="ef-wrap"><a href="#ef-priorities">Contact priorities</a><a href="#ef-checklist">Free template</a><a href="#ef-two-weeks">Two-week example</a><a href="#ef-handoff">Call &amp; handoff</a><a href="#ef-outcomes">Reporting</a><a href="#ef-scope">Campaign scope</a><a href="#ef-faq">Questions</a></div></nav>

  <section id="ef-priorities" class="ef-section"><div class="ef-wrap"><div class="ef-heading"><div><p class="ef-eyebrow">01 / Start with the person’s intent</p><h2>Follow up on what<br>actually happened.</h2></div><p>A demo request, a useful booth conversation and a badge scan each give the caller a different starting point.</p></div><div class="ef-situation-grid">{% for item in event.situations %}<article><p class="ef-label">{{ item.label }}</p><h3>{{ item.title }}</h3><p>{{ item.note }}</p><div class="ef-situation-action"><strong>The calling approach</strong><p>{{ item.action }}</p></div><p class="ef-next"><span>Possible next step</span>{{ item.next }}</p></article>{% endfor %}</div><div class="ef-rule"><strong>Keep the event context attached.</strong><p>The original notes stay with the record, so your buyer’s question survives the move from the booth to the sales meeting.</p></div></div></section>

  <section id="ef-checklist" class="ef-section ef-paper"><div class="ef-wrap ef-checklist-layout"><div><p class="ef-eyebrow">02 / Your event list, ready to work</p><h2>Give us the context<br>you already collected.</h2><p class="ef-body-lead">Start with your CRM export or spreadsheet. We review the fields, account ownership and missing details before outreach begins.</p><p>The free intake template gives your team one place to capture event notes, requests, ownership and follow-up tasks. Use it for your next show or to prepare a list you already have.</p><a class="ef-button" href="/assets/downloads/trade-show-follow-up-intake-template.csv" download="CallTeam-Event-Follow-Up-Template.csv" data-event-template>Download the Event Follow-Up Template <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a><p class="ef-caption">CSV for Excel or Google Sheets. Free, with no email gate. Fill it in within your own systems.</p></div><ol class="ef-checklist">{% for item in event.checklist %}<li><span>0{{ loop.index }}</span><div><h3>{{ item.title }}</h3><p>{{ item.text }}</p></div></li>{% endfor %}</ol></div></section>

  <section id="ef-two-weeks" class="ef-section"><div class="ef-wrap"><div class="ef-heading"><div><p class="ef-eyebrow">03 / An illustrative calling plan</p><h2>What the first<br>two weeks can look like.</h2></div><p>Calling and follow-up run together. People who ask to meet move into scheduling as soon as the qualification and calendar details are confirmed.</p></div><div class="ef-preflight"><strong>Before calling starts</strong><p>Approve the list, account exclusions, opening, requested materials, meeting standard and sales calendar access.</p></div><div class="ef-week-grid"><article><div class="ef-week-heading"><span>Week</span><strong>01</strong></div><h3>Reconnect with the event contacts.</h3><ol><li><strong>Work the clearest requests first.</strong><p>Call people who requested a demo, quote or callback, checking fit and existing sales ownership.</p></li><li><strong>Continue the documented conversations.</strong><p>Use the booth notes, deliver agreed information and schedule useful callbacks. Review badge-only records for suitable outreach.</p></li></ol></article><article><div class="ef-week-heading"><span>Week</span><strong>02</strong></div><h3>Follow through and hand over.</h3><ol><li><strong>Keep the commitments.</strong><p>Complete callbacks, handle replies and continue suitable unanswered contacts within the agreed sequence.</p></li><li><strong>Review the next step on every open record.</strong><p>Confirm meetings, pass buyer notes to sales and agree which contacts need later follow-up, another owner or closure.</p></li></ol></article></div><p class="ef-caption">An example covering ten working days after launch. Your proposal confirms start date, calling capacity and follow-up window; this is not a fixed package or a promise of meeting volume.</p><a class="ef-text-link" href="/b2b-cold-calling-campaign-process/">Planning ongoing prospecting too? See our first 60 days of calling <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></section>

  <section id="ef-handoff" class="ef-section ef-dark"><div class="ef-wrap ef-handoff-layout"><div><p class="ef-eyebrow">04 / From booth notes to a useful meeting</p><h2>Pick up the conversation<br>where your team left it.</h2><p class="ef-body-lead">The caller uses the buyer’s actual question and checks what still needs answering.</p><figure class="ef-call-example"><figcaption>Example opening / Use confirmed notes</figcaption><blockquote>“Hi [name], this is [caller] from CallTeam, calling on behalf of [company]. You spoke with [colleague] at [event] about [confirmed topic] and asked for [next step]. Is now a good time to pick that up?”</blockquote></figure><p>For a badge-only record, introduce the company and ask whether the event topic is relevant. Keep the opening accurate to what you know.</p><p class="ef-specialist">Your salesperson handles the deeper product discussion, proposal and closing. We provide the context and coordinate the next conversation.</p></div><article class="ef-handoff-card" aria-labelledby="ef-handoff-title"><div class="ef-sheet-top"><span>Sales handoff</span><span>Illustrative</span></div><h3 id="ef-handoff-title">A demo with a reason behind it.</h3><dl><div><dt>Event context</dt><dd>An operations director discussed manual reporting at your booth and asked to see a product example.</dd></div><div><dt>Confirmed need</dt><dd>They want to understand how reporting across two teams would work in one system.</dd></div><div><dt>Agreed meeting</dt><dd>A focused demo of that workflow with your product specialist.</dd></div><div><dt>Still to establish</dt><dd>Integration requirements, budget, buying timeline and other decision-makers.</dd></div><div><dt>Handoff owner</dt><dd>Your assigned salesperson receives the notes and runs the demo. CallTeam confirms the invitation and attendance details.</dd></div></dl><p class="ef-caption">A sample record, not a reported client result. The meeting purpose is agreed; commercial discovery continues with your team.</p></article></div></section>

  <section id="ef-outcomes" class="ef-section"><div class="ef-wrap ef-outcomes-layout"><div><p class="ef-eyebrow">05 / Reporting your team can use</p><h2>Know where the<br>event conversations stand.</h2><p class="ef-body-lead">See who was reached, what they said and who owns the next action.</p><p>We keep the event source attached to the campaign record. Reporting separates attempts, conversations, meetings booked and meetings held. Your team’s feedback adds sales acceptance and subsequent opportunity progress.</p><a class="ef-button" href="/b2b-meeting-quality-check/">Check Your Meeting Quality <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><p class="ef-caption">Use the tool to define and review meeting quality alongside your event campaign.</p></div><dl class="ef-outcomes">{% for item in event.outcomes %}<div><dt>{{ item.status }}</dt><dd><p>{{ item.meaning }}</p><strong>{{ item.action }}</strong></dd></div>{% endfor %}</dl></div></section>

  <section id="ef-scope" class="ef-section ef-paper"><div class="ef-wrap ef-scope-layout"><div><p class="ef-eyebrow">06 / Give the campaign a clear scope</p><h2>Start with one event.<br>Define the work.</h2><p class="ef-body-lead">Bring the list and tell us what a worthwhile sales conversation looks like. We’ll agree the audience, calling effort and handoff around it.</p><p>CallTeam manages list review, approved calling, follow-up, qualification, scheduling, confirmation and campaign reporting. Your team provides the offer, event context, approved materials and sellers ready to take the meetings.</p><p>Explore our <a href="/case-studies/">published appointment-setting case studies</a> to see how we document campaign work and outcomes.</p></div><aside class="ef-scope-card" aria-label="Event follow-up campaign scoping"><p class="ef-label">What your proposal will define</p><ul><li>Contact volume and data preparation</li><li>Markets, calling hours and follow-up channels</li><li>Priority groups and account exclusions</li><li>Calling capacity and campaign duration</li><li>Qualification, booking and sales handoff</li><li>Reporting, responsibilities and price</li></ul><a class="ef-button ef-button-solid" href="https://calendly.com/hello-callteam/new-meeting" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Scope Your Event Follow-Up <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><p class="ef-caption">For broader, ongoing outbound programs, <a href="/pricing/">review CallTeam’s managed-service pricing</a>.</p></aside></div><div class="ef-wrap ef-other-needs"><strong>Working a different lead source?</strong><p>Use <a href="/services/lead-reactivation/">Lead Reactivation</a> for older, dormant event lists, or the <a href="/articles/outsourced-inbound-lead-follow-up/">inbound follow-up guide</a> for a continuing flow of new website enquiries.</p></div></section>

  <section id="ef-faq" class="ef-section"><div class="ef-wrap ef-faq-layout"><div><p class="ef-eyebrow">Before you hand over the list</p><h2>Questions about<br>post-event follow-up.</h2><p>Agree the details while the event context is still fresh.</p></div><div class="ef-faqs">{% for faq in event.faqs %}<details><summary>{{ faq.q }}</summary><p>{{ faq.a }}</p></details>{% endfor %}</div></div></section>

  <section class="ef-section ef-final ef-paper"><div class="ef-wrap"><p class="ef-eyebrow">Put a team behind the next step</p><h2>Keep the conversation moving<br>after the event.</h2><p>Tell us which event you attended, what your team captured and who you want to meet. We’ll show you how CallTeam can take the follow-up forward.</p><a class="ef-button ef-button-solid" href="https://calendly.com/hello-callteam/new-meeting" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Plan Your Event Follow-Up <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><p class="ef-final-secondary"><a href="#contact">Prefer to write? Tell us about your event.</a></p></div></section>
